# Allowlist, not a denylist, and deliberately so.
#
# This repo holds a year of household load data and a .env with credentials. A denylist that
# forgets one pattern bakes either of those into an image layer, where it survives deletion
# of the file and is trivially readable with `docker history` / `docker save`. Starting from
# "send nothing" means a new data file added later is excluded by default rather than
# included by accident.
#
# Anything the container needs at runtime must be added here explicitly.
*

!*.py
!requirements.txt
!plan-now.sh
!solar-forecast.sh

# Never, under any circumstances - listed again after the allowlist as a second line of
# defence, in case a broader ! rule is added above and quietly re-admits them.
.env
.venv/
*.csv
*.excluded.json
price_cache/
pv_cache/
plans/
logs/
results/
results-raw-baseline/
entsoe-output*.txt
solarforecast.json
